      "purpose": "Defines the useSuspenseInfiniteQuery React hook, a Suspense-enabled variant of infinite query that wraps useBaseQuery with forced enabled/suspense and throws on error by default.",
      "summary": "The file exports a single React hook that provides Suspense support for infinite (paginated) queries. It performs a development-only check that skipToken is not used as the query function, then delegates to the base query hook with configuration that forces the query to be enabled, use suspense, and throw on error. The return value is cast to a success result type suitable for Suspense usage. It relies on external query-core observers and local base hook utilities.",
      "businessContext": "Part of TanStack React Query library. Enables unified Suspense data fetching for infinite lists in React. Failure breaks Suspense integration and paginated data loading.",
